(150, 1, NULL, 'assistant', '**CS Form No. 6 (Revised 2020)** is the official **Application for Leave** form used by government employees. It is accomplished in duplicate and contains sections for applicant details, specific leave details, and the official action taken on the application.\n\n### 1. Key Components of the Form\n*   **Applicant Details:** Name, office/department, date of filing, position, and salary.\n*   **Details of Application:** Type of leave, specific details (e.g., destination, illness, or purpose), number of working days applied for, inclusive dates, and commutation request (requested or not requested).\n*   **Details of Action:** Certification of leave credits (vacation and sick leave balances), recommendation for approval/disapproval, and the final approval/disapproval status by the authorized official.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Summary of Leave Types and Requirements\nThe form outlines specific guidelines and documentary requirements for various types of leaves:\n\n*   **Vacation Leave:** Must be filed 5 days in advance, when possible. Requires travel authority/clearance if traveling abroad.\n*   **Mandatory/Forced Leave:** Annual 5-day leave that is forfeited if not taken, unless cancelled due to exigency of service.\n*   **Sick Leave:** Filed immediately upon return. Requires a medical certificate (or affidavit if no medical consultation was made) if filed in advance or if exceeding 5 days.\n*   **Maternity Leave (105 days):** Requires proof of pregnancy (e.g., ultrasound or doctor\'s certificate) and a Notice of Allocation (CS Form No. 6a), if applicable.\n*   **Paternity Leave (7 days):** Requires proof of child\'s delivery (birth certificate, medical certificate, and marriage contract).\n*   **Special Privilege Leave (3 days):** Must be filed at least 1 week prior, except in emergencies.\n*   **Solo Parent Leave (7 days):** Filed 5 days in advance, when possible, with an updated Solo Parent ID.\n*   **Study Leave (up to 6 months):** Requires meeting internal agency requirements and a signed contract.\n*   **VAWC Leave (10 days):** Filed in advance or upon return. Requires a Protection Order (BPO/TPO/PPO), court/barangay certification, or a police report with a medical certificate.\n*   **Rehabilitation Leave (up to 6 months):** Application must be made within 1 week of the accident. Requires a letter request, police/medical reports, and government physician concurrence if a private doctor is used.\n*   **Special Leave Benefits for Women (up to 2 months):** For gynecological surgery. Must be filed 5 days prior (except emergencies) and accompanied by a comprehensive medical certificate and surgical reports.\n*   **Special Emergency (Calamity) Leave (up to 5 days):** Can be applied for within 30 days of a natural calamity. Granted once a year based on residency and official calamity declarations.\n*   **Monetization of Leave Credits:** Requesting 50% or more of accumulated credits requires a letter request stating valid reasons.\n*   **Terminal Leave:** Requires proof of resignation, retirement, or separation from service.\n*   **Adoption Leave:** Requires an authenticated copy of the Pre-Adoptive Placement Authority from the DSWD.\n\n*Note: Any leave of absence for thirty (30) calendar days or more, as well as terminal leave, requires clearance from money, property, and work-related accountabilities.*', '[{\"source_id\":24,\"source_name\":\"CS Form No. 6, Revised 2020 (Application for Leave) (Secured).pdf\",\"type\":\"pdf\"}]', '{\"provider\":\"gemini\",\"mode\":\"qa\"}', 0, '2026-05-19 17:21:13', '2026-05-19 17:21:13'),
