(152, 21, NULL, 'assistant', '**PETAlink** is a web-based digital portal designed for flower shop owners in Dagupan City to improve customer interaction, streamline business operations, and enhance the overall ordering workflow. \n\n### Key Features and Details:\n* **Purpose:** It addresses the challenges of manual and time-consuming processes in handling customer inquiries, browsing flower products, and coordinating orders.\n* **Maps API Integration:** Allows customers to view physical locations of participating flower shops, helping them easily identify and navigate to nearby shops.\n* **Development Methodology:** Developed using the Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC), specifically the Rapid Application Development (RAD) methodology, to allow for continuous user feedback and rapid refinement.\n* **Usability and Evaluation:** Evaluated using the System Usability Scale (SUS), scoring highly in usability (4.76), design (4.78), navigation (4.78), and user-friendliness (4.80).\n* **Target Users:** Features dedicated interfaces and pages for customers (e.g., cart, checkout, orders), shop owners (e.g., profile, feedback, reports), and administrators (e.g., dashboard, verification, managing owners/customers).', '[{\"source_id\":25,\"source_name\":\"PETAlink_Manuscript_KathStone.pdf\",\"type\":\"pdf\"}]', '{\"provider\":\"gemini\",\"mode\":\"qa\"}', 0, '2026-05-19 17:32:26', '2026-05-19 17:32:26'),
