(156, 1, NULL, 'assistant', 'Based on the provided document context, here is a summary of the information from the selected files:\n\n### 1. CS Form No. 6, Revised 2020 (Application for Leave)\nThis document is the official Civil Service Form No. 6 (Revised 2020) used by government employees in the Republic of the Philippines to apply for various types of leaves. \n\n**Key Components of the Form:**\n*   **Applicant Details:** Includes fields for Office/Department, Name, Date of Filing, Position, and Salary.\n*   **Leave Details:** Sections to specify the type of leave, details of the leave (e.g., destination if abroad, specific illness, or purpose of study leave), number of working days applied for, and commutation requests.\n*   **Action on Application:** Sections for the Certification of Leave Credits (by an authorized officer), Recommendation (Approval/Disapproval), and final Approval/Disapproval by the authorized official.\n\n**Summary of Leave Types and Requirements:**\n*   **Vacation Leave:** Must be filed 5 days in advance when possible. Requires travel authority/clearance if spent abroad.\n*   **Mandatory/Forced Leave:** Annual 5-day leave that is forfeited if not taken, unless cancelled due to exigency of service.\n*   **Sick Leave:** Must be filed immediately upon return. Requires a medical certificate if it exceeds 5 days or is filed in advance.\n*   **Maternity Leave (105 days):** Requires proof of pregnancy (e.g., ultrasound or doctor\'s certificate).\n*   **Paternity Leave (7 days):** Requires proof of child\'s delivery (e.g., birth certificate, marriage contract).\n*   **Special Privilege Leave (3 days):** Must be filed at least 1 week prior, except in emergencies.\n*   **Solo Parent Leave (7 days):** Must be filed 5 days in advance when possible; requires an updated Solo Parent ID.\n*   **Study Leave (up to 6 months):** Requires meeting internal agency requirements and a formal contract.\n*   **VAWC (Violence Against Women and Their Children) Leave (10 days):** Requires a Protection Order (BPO/TPO/PPO), court/barangay certification, or a police report with a medical certificate.\n*   **Rehabilitation Leave (up to 6 months):** For job-related injuries; must be applied for within 1 week of the accident with supporting medical and police reports.\n*   **Special Leave Benefits for Women (up to 2 months):** For gynecological surgeries; must be filed 5 days in advance (except in emergencies) with a medical certificate and clinical summary.\n*   **Special Emergency (Calamity) Leave (up to 5 days):** Can be applied for within 30 days of a natural calamity/disaster affecting the employee\'s residence.\n*   **Monetization of Leave Credits:** Requires a formal letter request to the head of the agency for requests of 50% or more of accumulated credits.\n*   **Terminal Leave:** Requires proof of resignation, retirement, or separation from service.\n*   **Adoption Leave:** Requires an authenticated copy of the Pre-Adoptive Placement Authority from the DSWD.\n\n*Note: Any leave of absence lasting 30 calendar days or more, as well as terminal leave, requires clearance from money, property, and work-related accountabilities.*\n\n---\n\n### 2. Agra AMICUS 2026.pdf\nThere is no text or content provided in the document context for this file. Consequently, no summary can be generated for it.', '[{\"source_id\":24,\"source_name\":\"CS Form No. 6, Revised 2020 (Application for Leave) (Secured).pdf\",\"type\":\"pdf\"},{\"source_id\":23,\"source_name\":\"Agra AMICUS 2026.pdf\",\"type\":\"pdf\"},{\"source_id\":21,\"source_name\":\"Agra AMICUS 2026.pdf\",\"type\":\"pdf\"}]', '{\"provider\":\"gemini\",\"mode\":\"qa\"}', 0, '2026-05-19 22:38:13', '2026-05-19 22:38:13'),
