(196, 23, NULL, 'assistant', 'Heneral Luna refers to **General Antonio Luna y Novicio**, a prominent Filipino general who fought in the Philippine-American War. He is considered one of the fiercest and most brilliant military leaders of his time.\n\nHere\'s a bit more about him:\n*   **Full Name and Background:** His full name was Antonio Narciso Luna de San Pedro y Novicio Ancheta. He was born on October 29, 1866, in San Nicolas, Manila, and came from a privileged family. He was also the youngest of seven children, and his older brother was the famous painter Juan Luna.\n*   **Education and Early Career:** Luna was a highly educated individual, studying pharmacy and earning a Bachelor of Arts degree. He also pursued further studies in Belgium and France, where he worked at the Pasteur Institute. He was commissioned by the Spanish government to study tropical and communicable diseases and became the chief chemist of the Municipal Laboratory of Manila.\n*   **Role in the Revolution:** Antonio Luna was a key figure in the Propaganda Movement, writing for *La Solidaridad* under the pen name \"Taga-ilog.\" He later joined the Philippine Revolutionary forces and became a brigadier general. He was appointed as Chief of War Operations and eventually the Director or Assistant Secretary of War and Supreme Chief of the Republican Army.\n*   **Military Acumen:** Luna was known for his military genius, strict discipline, and strategic thinking. He organized professional guerrilla soldiers known as the \"Luna Sharpshooters\" and the \"Black Guard.\" His \"Luna Defense Line\" was a significant challenge for American troops during their campaign north of Manila.\n*   **Temper and Assassination:** He was also known for his fiery temper and uncompromising nature, which sometimes led to conflicts with other leaders. Tragically, he was assassinated on June 5, 1899, at the age of 32. His death is considered a decisive factor in the fight against American forces, with some believing his scientific approach to war could have saved the islands from American imperialism.\n*   **Legacy:** General Frederick Funston, an American general, even regarded Luna as the \"ablest and most aggressive leader of the Filipino Republic.\" His life and contributions were also depicted in the 2015 historical film \"Heneral Luna,\" which brought his story to a wider audience.', '[{\"source_id\":null,\"source_name\":\"wikipedia.org\",\"type\":\"web\",\"source_url\":\"https:\\/\\/vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com\\/grounding-api-redirect\\/AUZIYQEFIp4Ic3f-soqHJKe5bTs-b521BA7pU4ZFwuOhX2B1p6LMXWszAAGYYzMqMNf3oHq6MIS1OOevhuvf18hFJKZipL3D12OKFXIrzISlXL4xxmUGunH7Ab-MRbTU0eSf-VusjTXHhg==\"},{\"source_id\":null,\"source_name\":\"youtube.com\",\"type\":\"web\",\"source_url\":\"https:\\/\\/vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com\\/grounding-api-redirect\\/AUZIYQHFUreNZP1SbGdSyi8es2xz729U7829qTvsDieKjbsSW18xxvgWNEWGoz09Ak58udI81LQp-DWwmlz5R85rwBGbCiTAxp2Y1wF5z0YImDGuOMa71M3Hl3_CyWMH5Qx0BkkZrYS-Wg0=\"},{\"source_id\":null,\"source_name\":\"nyu.edu\",\"type\":\"web\",\"source_url\":\"https:\\/\\/vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com\\/grounding-api-redirect\\/AUZIYQHx40yr3hdH76mwnCTyT7spdYuTCdlKXzsaZKe5YJmf7gqRAN-HYjKtNBevU9K-avWXzFZsI7UypzgeLQmbuqB-j2J0QoSvvraYunNFMTXBo-AUIG1DvbNhovJEJECkqlbtnFTdBfzOMML7nBrQLBgMxGZK8tq0Gz0SV_dXkcrW4w==\"},{\"source_id\":null,\"source_name\":\"familysearch.org\",\"type\":\"web\",\"source_url\":\"https:\\/\\/vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com\\/grounding-api-redirect\\/AUZIYQFigKgwnKlkXOWXuNPOhwiVBtIZvNEH3ygIXfnE4j0_ORRNRkddf5zTfmtzhDpquEhqZQ0FVCHgN9F-M_M8G-g7x8JLotPEXrzCQOCi17eXXe5KVXQ7f6VSHdOQ2gk_s1-XK36ymEAuzJynOd3KwX6olQ1MH0mps-Ga82ArGbdvPY86t-bUupG2qk63MgcCdzw=\"},{\"source_id\":null,\"source_name\":\"nema.gov.mn\",\"type\":\"web\",\"source_url\":\"https:\\/\\/vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com\\/grounding-api-redirect\\/AUZIYQGnXrNQ0l7fDh72tQ2UU933iuenKPDu0ZtJ6BTjnF8OdY9921Ujq846_NnTPl0MTCVA5gjJqAfvmWGiCAbwtLvPFMOiY5lFfULcqZWfEswOn7O25ZJ4SDHhD3QeIScYk8EXvzegYmTjULFN