logyEducation UniversidaddeDagupan ArellanoSt.,DagupanCity BACHELOROFSCIENCEININFORMATIONTECHNOLOGY DAROY,KATHLEENCHARMQ. MEDRANO,PATRICKS. SORIANO,RAHMYRHICSSONL. ZARENO,MARKEZEKIELG. December2025 ii APPROVALSHEET InpartialfulfillmentoftherequirementsleadingtothedegreeofBACHELOR OFSCIENCEININFORMATIONTECHNOLOGY,thecompletedprojectstudy entitled,PETAlink:AnOnlineCustomerDigitalPortalforFlowerShopOwnersin DagupanCity,preparedandsubmittedbyDaroy,KathleenCharmQ.,Zareno,Mark EzekielG.,Medrano,PatrickS.,Soriano,RahmYrhicssonL.,isendorsedfor approvalandacceptance. KYLEDITRIG.MORENO,MIT Adviser Thisistocertifythatthecompletedprojectstudymentionedabovesubmittedby Daroy,KathleenCharmQ.,Zareno,MarkEzekielG.,Medrano,PatrickS.,Soriano, RahmYrhicssonL.,hasbeenexaminedandapprovedonDECEMBER15,2025bythe OralExaminationCommittee. JANNALFREDA.QUINTO,MSIB Chairman EVANGELINEN.LACHICA,MIT BENITAL.BIALA,MIT Member Member ROBERTHS.LLOREN Member Acceptedandapprovedaspartialfulfillmentoftherequirementsforthe degreeofBACHELOROFSCIENCEININFORMATIONTECHNOLOGYon DECEMBER15.2025,withaGradeofPASSED. JANNALFREDA.QUINTO,MSIB Dean,SchoolofInformationTechnologyEducation iii ABSTRACT KathleenCharmQ.Daroy,PatrickS.Medrano,RahmYrhicssonL.Soriano,Mark EzekielG.Zareno,PETAlink:AnOnlineCustomerDigitalPortalforFlowerShop OwnersinDagupanCity,BachelorofScienceinInformationTechnology,Schoolof InformationTechnologyEducation,UniversidaddeDagupan,ArellanoSt.,DagupanCity, Pangasinan,Philippines. Adviser:KYLEDITRIG.MORENO,MIT ThiscapstonestudypresentsthedevelopmentandevaluationofPetaLink:An OnlineCustomerDigitalPortalforFlowerShopOwnersinDagupanCity,aweb-based systemdesignedtoimprovecustomerinteractionandoperationalefficiencyamonglocal flowershops.Thestudyaddressesthechallengesofmanualandtime-consuming processesinhandlingcustomerinquiries,browsingofflowerproducts,andorder coordination.ByintegratingMapsAPI,thesystemallowsuserstoviewthephysical locationsofparticipatingflowershops,helpingcustomerseasilyidentifynearbyshops andnavigatetotheirpreferredlocations.Thisfeatureenhancesaccessibilityandlocation awareness,supportingbetterservicecoordinationandimprovingtheoveralluser experiencebyprovidingaccurateandinteractivemap-basedinformationwithinthe platform.UsingtheSoftwareDevelopmentLifeCycle(SDLC)—specificallytheRapid ApplicationDevelopment(RAD)methodology—thedevelopersfollowedaniterative approachconsistingofanalysisandquickdesign,prototypedevelopment,testing,and implementation.Thisapproachenabledcontinuoususerfeedback,fasterdevelopment cycles,andtimelyrefinementofsystemfeaturestoensurethatPetaLinkmetthe functionalandusabilityrequirementsofflowershopownersandcustomers.Theusability ofPetaLink:AnOnlineCustomerDigitalPortalforFlowerShopOwnersinDagupan CitywasevaluatedusingtheSystemUsabilityScale(SUS)withWeightedMeanand LikertScale.Thesystemscoredhighinusability(4.76),design(4.78),navigation(4.78), anduser-friendliness(4.80),indicatingitisintuitive,visuallyappealing,andeasytouse. TheseresultsdemonstratethatPetaLinkenhancestheorderingworkflowforboth customersandshopowners.Thedevelopersrecommendfutureenhancementsincludinga brighter,moreappealinguserinterface,adedicatedmobileapplication,expansion beyondDagupanCity,subscription-basedselleraccounts,acustomer-assistancechatbot, andintegrationofsecureonlinepaymentoptionstofurtherimproveusability, accessibility,andoverallfunctionality. Keywords:SystemUsabilityScale(SUS),RapidApplicationDevelopment(RAD),Web- BasedPortal,MapsAPI,DigitalOrderingSystem,CustomerManagement iv ACKNOWLEDGEMENT Firstandforemost,wegivethankstoGodAlmighty,thesourceofourstrength, wisdom,andperseverancethroughoutthisproject.Wewouldliketoexpressourdeepest gratitudetoourformeradviser,Mr.YuriRancudo,forhisguidanceandsupportduring theinitialphaseofthisstudy.Oursincereappreciationisextendedtoouradviser,Mr. KyleditriG.Moreno,forhiscontinuousguidance,constructivefeedback,and encouragement.Wearealsothankfultoourtechnicaladviser,Mr.BenjieF.Zarate, whoseexpertiseandassistancesignif