mandTikTok.DelaCruz(2022)furtheremphasizesthatlifestyle-driven spendinghasincreasedduetotheinfluenceofsocialmedia,especiallyforvisually pleasinggiftssuchasflowers. 2 Despitetheriseofdigitalplatforms,severalbarriershindertraditionalflower shopsfromtransitioningonline.AccordingtoStaff(2024),whiledigitalplatformswiden customerreach,itbecomesmoredifficultforbusinessestounderstandandengagetheir nichetargetaudience.Magsambol(2021)pointsoutthatdigitalilliteracy,lackoftraining, andpoorlogisticssupportareamongthemostsignificantobstaclesfacedbyFilipino SMEsenteringe-commerce. Additionally,CarreonandVillanueva(2023)foundthatover60%ofrural businessesinthePhilippinesremainunawareofavailabledigitaltoolsthatcould improvetheiroperations.TheU.S.DepartmentofCommerce(2024)alsonotesthat manySMEsinthePhilippineslackbasicdigitalinfrastructure,makingthemvulnerable inanincreasinglyonlinemark. However,adoptingdigitalsystemscansignificantlyimproveoperations. CastilloandRamos(2020)observedthatimplementingcloud-basedPOSandinventory systemshelpedflowershopsinBulacanimprovedeliveryaccuracyandspeed.These toolsalsostreamlinedcustomerinteractionsandminimizederrorsinstockhandling. Giventheseinsights,thePETAlinkplatformisdevelopedasaspecializedonlinesystem tailoredforflowershops.AccordingtoSuLattPhyu(2024),anidealonlineflowershop systemshouldincludefeaturessuchasreal-timeinventorytracking,customer management,digitalordering,andseamlesspaymentintegration.Auser-friendlysystem likePETAlinkcanempowerlocalflowershopownerstomodernizetheirbusiness operationsandreachmorecustomersefficiently. AccordingtoRepublicActNo.10844,Section2,theStaterecognizesthevital 3 roleofinformationandcommunicationstechnologyinnation-buildingandits potentialtoimprovethequalityoflifeofFilipinos.Italsoemphasizestheneedto developandpromotetheuseofICTforthedeliveryofefficientandeffective governmentservices. PetaLinkaddressesSDG8–DecentWorkandEconomicGrowth,which promotessustained,inclusive,andsustainableeconomicgrowthandproductive employment,byservingasanonlinecustomerdigitalportalforflowershopownersin DagupanCitythatenablesefficientordermanagement,customerinteraction,and streamlinedbusinessoperations,therebyhelpingsmallbusinessesincreaseproductivity, improveincomeopportunities,andsustaindecentwork;itsupportsSDG9–Industry, Innovation,andInfrastructure,whichfocusesonresilientinfrastructure,inclusive industrialization,andinnovation,asatechnology-drivenplatformthatmodernizes traditionalflowershopservices,promotinginnovation,accessibility,andoperational efficiencyamonglocalenterprises;itcontributestoSDG11–SustainableCitiesand Communities,whichaimstomakecitiesinclusive,safe,resilient,andsustainable,by empoweringcommunity-basedflowershopsthroughdigitalcommercesolutions, strengtheninglocalcommerceandsustainablecommunityenterprises;itaddressesSDG 12–ResponsibleConsumptionandProduction,whichencouragessustainableresource use,throughaccurateordertracking,inventorymanagement,andcoordinationof resources,reducingwasteandpromotingresponsiblebusinesspractices;itsupportsSDG 17–PartnershipsfortheGoals,whichemphasizesstrengtheningpartnershipsfor sustainabledevelopment,byprovidingadigitalplatformthatfacilitatescollaborationand 4 communicationbetweenflowershopownersandcustomers,fosteringcooperation, strongerbusinessnetworks,andcommunityengagement. Byintegratingkeydigitaltoolsintoasingle,accessibleplatform,PETAlinkaims toaddressexistingbarrierssuchaslowdigitalawareness,weaklogistics,andlackof systemautomation.Itplaysakeyroleinhelpinglocalflowershopsnotonlysurvivebut alsothriveintheevolvingdigitaleconomyofthePhilippinesandbeyond. StatementoftheObjectives Thisstudyfocusedonthedevelopedsystem,aweb-basedsystemdesignedto enableuserstobrowse,select,andorderflowerproductsefficiently.Specifically,the studysoughtto: 1.Toidentifytheexistingprocessesoftheflowershopowners; 2.Todescribethefeaturesofthedevelopedsystem;and 3.Totesttheusabilityofthedevelopedsystem. ConceptualFramework Tostructurethedevelopmentprocess,thedevelopersemployedtheRapid ApplicationDevelopment(RAD)model,aflexible,user-centeredsoftwaredevelopment methodologyintroducedbyMartin(1991)andsupportedbymorerecentwork (Dogiparthi,2019;Khoirunnisaetal.,2023).Ratherthanfollowingarigid,sequential flow,RADemphasizesquickdesigncycles,iterativeprototyping,andcontinuoususer feedback.Thismodelwaschosenbecausethesystemrequiresinteractivefeaturessuch asproductbrowsing,Cash-On-Deliverypaymentintegration,andordertrackingthat 5 benefitfromearlytestingandrefinement.RADallowsthedeveloperstoadjustfeatures basedonstakeholderinputthroughouttheprocess,ensuringthatthefinalproductmeets bothfunctionalandexperientialexpectations. ThestudyutilizedtheIPOmodel,TheInput-Process-Output(IPO)modelserves asafoundationalframeworkinsystemsdevelopmentandinformationsystemsdesign.It providesastructuredwayofunderstandinghowdata(input)istransformedthrough specificoperations(process)intomeaningfulresults(output).Thismodelisespecially valuableindesigningdigitalplatformssuchase-commercewebsitesorcustomerportals, whereuserinteractionsgeneratedatathatmustbeprocessedefficientlytoproduce accurateandvaluableservices.AccordingtoPereraetal.(2017),titled“TheUseofan Input-Process-OutputFrameworktoUnderstandUrbanEnvironmentalMonitoring Systems”,appliedtheIPOmodeltoanalyzehowsensor-baseddata(input)was processedthroughcomputationalalgorithms(process)toproduceactionable environmentalreports(output).ThestudydemonstratedhowtheIPOframeworkhelped identifybottlenecksindataaccuracyandreportingspeed,ultimatelyleadingto improvementsinreal-timeurbanenvironmentalmonitoring. Theconceptualframeworkbeginswiththeinputstage,wheredataiscollected fromshopowners,employees,andpotentialusersthroughplanningsessions,interviews, andsurveys.Theseinputshelpedidentifyoperationalchallengesanddefinethespecific featuresandfunctionsthesystemmustsupport. Intheprocessstage,thephasesoftheRADmodelareapplied.Initialanalysisand quickdesignactivitiesshapedthesystem’searlystructurebasedonthegathered 6 requirements.Thisisfollowedbyaseriesofprototypingcyclesbuild,demonstrate,and refinewheresystemmodulesaredeveloped,tested,andimprovedwithdirectuser involvement.Testingisconductedcontinuouslytovalidateeachcomponent,leadingup tofullimplementation,followedbyverificationandmaintenancetoensurereliabilityand long-termfunctionality. ThefinaloutputisPETAlink,anonlinecustomerdigitalportalforflowershop ownersthatstreamlineskeytaskssuchasorderhandling,andcustomertransactions.This frameworksupportsaniterative,user-focuseddevelopmentstrategythatensuresthefinal productdirectlyaddressedthepracticalchallengesidentifiedduringtheinputphase. Figure1.1ResearchParadigmofPETAlink:AnOnlineCustomerDigitalPortalforFlowerShopOwnersinDagupanCity 8 ScopeandLimitations PETAlinkisanonlinecustomerdigitalportalforflowershopinthevicinityof DagupanCity.PETAlinkisaweb-basedflowershopsystemthatconnectsflowershop ownersandcustomersthroughanonlineportalallowingcustomerstobrowse,select, andorderawidevarietyofflowerarrangementsandrelatedproducts.Thesystem includedessentialfeaturessuchasaninternalsitesearch,flowercatalogmanagement, shoppingcartandcheckoutfunctionality,Cash-on-Deliveryandpickuppayment options,geolocationintegration,customerreviewsandratings,orderstatusand notifications,accountinformationmanagement,andasalesreportingfeatureforshop owners. Additionally,thesystem’sgeneralfunctionalitywasinfluencedbyseveral limitations,suchasbeinglimitedtotheoperationofflowershopswithinDagupanCity only,whichsignificantlyhinderednationwideaccessibility.Deliverywashandledsolely bytheflowershopsthemselvesandwasnotmanagedortrackedbythesystem.The portalalsolackedafullyintegratedonlinepaymentgatewayandinsteadreliedonCash- on-DeliveryandPick-Uppaymentoptionsfortransactions.Thisworkaroundwas implementedduetothecomplexityandsecuritydemandsinvolvedindevelopingand maintainingacomprehensiveonlinepaymentsystem.Furthermore,thesystemhadno nativemobileapplicationintegration,whichlimitedmobileoptimization,offlineaccess, andoverallconvenienceforusers. 9 SignificanceoftheStudy Thisstudywouldbebeneficialtothefollowing: DagupanCity.TheimplementationofthePETAlinksystemcontributestothe advancementoflocalbusinessesinDagupanCitybyintroducingdigitalsolutions specificallytailoredtotheflowershopindustry.Itsupportsthecity\'sprogresstoward digitalizationandinnovationinsmallandmediumenterprises. FlowerShops.Thesystemoffersanorganizedandefficientplatformfor managingproductlistings,customerorders,andonlinetransactions.Ithelpsmodernize traditionalflowershopoperationsandimprovesoverallservicequality. FlowerShopOwners.Ownerswillbenefitfromautomatedprocessessuchas orderhandling,inventorycontrol,andcustomerengagement.Thisreducesoperational costs,minimizeserrors,andincreasestheircapacitytoservemorecustomers,helping themstaycompetitiveintheonlinemarket. Employees.Employeeswillgainaccesstoamorestructuredandmanageable workflow.Thesystemreducesrepetitivemanualtasksandallowsstafftofocusonmore value-addedservices,resultinginimprovedproductivityandjobsatisfaction. Customers.Customerswillenjoyamoreconvenientanduser-friendlyexperience throughtheonlineplatform.Theycaneasilybrowseflowerarrangements,place customizedorders,andtrackdeliveries,resultinginasmootherandmoresatisfying shoppingprocess. Developers.Thisstudyenhancesthetechnicalskillsofdevelopersbyproviding real-worldexperienceindesigningandimplementingbusiness-specificsystems.It 10 emphasizesintegratingkeycomponentssuchasinventorymanagement,customer interfaces,andsecurepaymentfeatures. FutureResearchersandDevelopers.Thestudyservesasavaluablereference forfutureacademicandsystemdevelopmentprojects.Itcontributestoongoingresearch inthefieldsofe-commerce,localizeddigitalsolutions,andthetechnological empowermentofsmallbusinesses. DefinitionofTerms Toensureclarityandconsistencythroughoutthestudy,thefollowingkeyterms aredefinedastheyareusedinthecontextofthisresearch: ApplicationProgrammingInterface(API).Integratedtoallowflowershop ownerstopintheirexactshoplocation.Thislocationisdisplayedon