rates. KimandPark(2022)analyzedSouthKoreanonlinefloralservicesandtheiruse ofreal-timecustomizationoptions.Theirstudyrevealedthatenablingusersto personalizebouquetsanddeliverydetailsenhancedusersatisfactionandincreased repeatpurchaseratesbynearly20%. PataragusandWijaya(2023)assessedthetechnologicalinfrastructurebehind Indonesia’sleadingflorale-commerceplatforms.TheyfoundthatAPIsandcentralized 14 ordermanagementsystemsledtomorestandardizedprocesses,whichsignificantly reduceddeliveryerrorsandimprovedcoordinationamongvendors.Locally,Natividad (2023)examinedhowe-commerceplatformshavesupportedmicroentrepreneursinthe plantandflowerindustry,particularlyaftertheCOVID-19pandemic.Thestudy revealedthatonlinesellingempoweredsmallvendorsbyextendingtheircustomerbase andminimizingrelianceonphysicalshops. Reyna(2023)developedaLaravel-basedcapstonesystemcalledFlowerHub, whichintegratesproductcataloging,ordermonitoring,andpaymentfeatures.Thesystem recordedahighSystemUsabilityScale(SUS)score,indicatingseamlessfunctionality andusersatisfaction. Lindawan(2022)exploredthedigitaltransformationofClark’sFlowerShop,a traditionalfloralbusinessthatmigratedfrommanualoperationstoanonlineordering system.Thetransitionledtoimprovementsincustomerserviceefficiencyandsales consistency. ReyesandNavarra(2022)conductedaqualitativecasestudyexploringFilipino consumers\'perceptionsofonlineflowerorderingsystems.Respondentshighlightedthe importanceofhavingclearlydefinedorderingstepsandreliabledeliveryservicesto fostercustomertrust. Aretaetal.(2015)assessedthecurrentstatusanddevelopmentpotentialofflower shopsinBatangasCity.Theirstudyaimedtosupportvendorsinenhancingprofitability andmarketingstrategiesbyidentifyingkeyareasforbusinessdevelopmentandconsumer engagement. 15 Onlineflowershopssignificantlytransformedthefloralretailindustryby replacingtraditionalface-to-facetransactionswithdigitalexperiences,makingiteasier forcustomerstopurchasefreshflowersandencouragingmorefrequentonlinebuying habits.Manybusinessesadop