aturesimproveusability,convenience,andoverallsatisfactionforbothcustomersand shopowners. Theusabilitytest,conductedusingtheSystemUsabilityScale(SUS)with WeightedMeanandLikertScale,showedpositiveresultsforPetaLink:AnOnline CustomerDigitalPortalforFlowerShopOwnersinDagupanCity.Thesystemachieved highscoresinusability(4.76),design(4.78),navigation(4.78),anduser-friendliness (4.80),indicatingthatusersfinditeasytouse,visuallyappealing,andintuitive.These resultsconfirmthatPetaLinkprovidesasmooth,efficient,anduser-friendlyexperience, improvingtheorderingworkflowforbothcustomersandshopowners. 79 Conclusion Thisstudyexploredthedevelopmentandevaluationofaweb-basedflowershop systemaimedatimprovingtheefficiencyofbrowsing,selecting,andorderingflower products. Throughthissystem,ithelpsthecustomersandshopownersminimizedelaysand inefficiencies,asthefindingsrevealedthattheexistingprocessesofflowershopowners arelargelymanual,time-consuming,andpronetosetbacks,particularlyinorderhandling andcustomerinquiries. Throughthefeaturesofthesystem,suchasproductbrowsing,orderplacement, useraccountmanagement,andsystemnotifications,operationalefficiencyis significantlyimproved.Thesefeaturesprovideshopownersandcustomerswithamore organizedandconvenienttransactionexperience,reducingmanualworkloadand enhancingservicedelivery. ThroughtheusabilitytestingconductedusingtheSystemUsabilityScale(SUS), thedevelopersidentifiedareasforimprovementandgathereduserfeedback.Users evaluatedtheinterfaceandfounditintuitive,easytonavigate,andefficientfor completingtasks,withhighscoresinusability(4.76),design(4.78),navigation(4.78), anduser-friendliness(4.80).Thesepositiveresultsindicatethatthesystemmeetsthe expectationsofitsintendedusersandissuitableforreal-worldimplementation. 80 Recommendation Thedevelopersrecommendthatcustomersaccessthesystemusingalaptopor desktopcomputer.Additionally,shopownersareadvisedtohaveessentialequipment, includingalaptopordesktopcomputer,astableinternetconnection,andareliableserver orhostingservicetostoreandmanagethesystem’sdata.Theseresourcesensureefficient managementofshopinformation,productlistings,andcustomertransactions. Thedevelopersrecommendthattheadminandemployeesfamiliarizethemselves withthefeaturesandcapabilitiesofthesystem.Understandingtheworkflow,tools,and managementfunctionswillpromotesmoothoperations,quickissueresolution,and consistentservicedelivery. Thedevelopersrecommendthatfuturedevelopersenhancethesystem’suser interfacebyadoptingabrighterandmorevisuallyappealingdesign.Theyalso recommenddevelopingadedicatedmobileapplication,expandingthesystem’scoverage beyondDagupanCity,subscriptionformembershipfeeforselleraccountregistration, chatbotforcustomerassistance,andintegratingsecureonlinepaymentoptionsto improveaccessibility,usability,andoverallfunctionality. 81 Bibliography Winter,D.(2024,August12).WhatisEcommerce?TheCompleteGuidetoonline selling(2024)-shopifyPhilippines.Shopify.RetrievedOctober8,2024,12:19P.M. Availableathttps://www.shopify.com/ph/blog/what-is-ecommerce Visa.(2021,March18).MoreFilipinosusee-commerceforthefirsttimeduetothe pandemic–Visastudy.Visa.https://www.visa.com.ph/about-visa/newsroom/press- releases/more-filipinos-use-ecommerce-for-the-first-time-due-to-the-pandemic-visa- study.html Desiderio,L.(2024,June3).Philippinese-commercemarkettoreach P2.2 trillion in 2028. ThePhilippineStar. https://www.philstar.com/business/2024/06/03/2359867/philippines-e-commerce- market-reach-p22-trillion-2028 Lantican,J.,&Ong,R.(2021).Pandemicpush:OnlinestorefrontsandFilipinoSMEs. AsianJournalofE-Commerce,7(3),120–132. https://doi.org/10.32945/ajec.2021.7.3.012 Rahmawati,N.,Sari,I.,&Putri,A.(2021).Trendsinfloralgiftingandsocialmedia influenceamongmillennials.JournalofConsumerStudies,15(2),45–53. https://doi.org/10.1093/jcs/jcs152045 DelaCruz,K.(2022).Thesocialmediaeffectonlifestyle-basedspendinginthe Philippines.MediaandMarketStudies,11(2),77–85. 82 Staff,S.(2024,January17).13ecommercechallengesandhowtoovercomethem(2024) -shopifyPhilippine